{
  "name": "Validate QR tickets in real time with n8n Forms and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automated QR Ticket Scanner & Validator\n\nDoor staff scan tickets into an n8n form on their phone and see the result immediately. Every scan is checked against your participant database, logged to a Scan Results sheet, and bad scans trigger an email alert.\n\n### Results staff see\n- ✅ **VALID**: admit the attendee\n- ⚠️ **ALREADY USED**: this ticket was already admitted at this checkpoint today\n- ❌ **INVALID**: the code isn't in the participant database\n- ⛔ **NOT ALLOWED**: the ticket exists but a rule blocks it (cancelled, wrong day, or wrong area)\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Connect Google Sheets credentials to **Read Participant Database**, **Read Scan Results**, and **Log Scan**\n- [ ] **Read Participant Database**: select your master participant sheet\n- [ ] **Read Scan Results** and **Log Scan**: select the same Scan Results sheet. An empty tab is fine; columns are created on the first scan.\n- [ ] **Validate Ticket**: check the settings at the top (ticket column, name column, and rule columns)\n- [ ] **Send Alert**: connect Gmail and set the recipient\n- [ ] Activate the workflow and open the **Ticket Scanner** production URL on each phone\n\n### Checkpoints\nAdd `?checkpoint=VIP%20Area` to the form URL to scan at a specific area. Without it, scans are logged as `Main Entrance`. Duplicate checks and area rules are per checkpoint.\n\n### Field scanning\nOpen the form on an Android phone, tap the field, and scan with a keyboard scanner app such as **Scan to Web**. Tap **Scan next ticket** on the result page to scan again.",
        "height": 1056,
        "width": 560
      },
